-- title:
--   Existence of a dictionary family of level-preserving isogenies
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, natural numbers $N \neq 0$ and $n > 0$ with $r \nmid n$ and $r \nmid N$, an algebraically closed field $k_0$ in which $N$ is invertible, an order $\Lambda$ in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ (containing $1$, closed under multiplication, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning and finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$) with $\mathbb{Z} \subseteq \Lambda$, and a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of level $N$ over $k_0$ with $\Lambda$-action. Assume further: a scheme $A$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k_0$ with structure morphism $f$ and a relative group law $L$; an order $O$ in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d]$ together with an injective map $\varepsilon$ from $O$ to endomorphisms of $A$ over $f$ which is additive on points, sends $1$ to the identity, satisfies $\varepsilon(xy) = \varepsilon(y)$ followed by $\varepsilon(x)$, and whose members are homomorphisms for $L$; a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $j : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ with $j(\Lambda) \subseteq M_2(O)$; morphisms $p_1, p_2 : A_0.A \to A$ over $k_0$ exhibiting $A_0.A$ as the fibre product of $f$ with itself and respecting the group laws; a family $E$ assigning to each matrix $y \in M_2(O)$ an endomorphism of $A_0.A$ over $A_0.f$, which is a homomorphism for $A_0.L$, sends $1$ to the identity, satisfies $E(yy') = E(y')$ followed by $E(y)$, is additive on points, recovers the $\Lambda$-action via $A_0.\mathrm{act}(m) = E(j(m))$, and whose components along $p_1, p_2$ are given by the $\varepsilon$ of the matrix entries; an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\tau : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ whose image is exactly the centraliser of $j(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])$, and an order $R$ in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ with $x \in R \iff \tau(x) \in M_2(O)$; a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $R'$ such that a unit $x$ lies in $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R', v)$ (the intersection over $w \neq v$ of the preimages under the local embeddings of the subgroups generated by the local boxes of $R'$) precisely when there are $K, K'$ with $r^K x, r^{K'} x^{-1} \in R$ and with $E(\tau(r^K x))$ and $E(\tau(r^{K'} x^{-1}))$ both carrying points factoring through $A_0.\mathrm{lev}$ to such points; and a subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ with $\Gamma_t = u\,\mathrm{awayUnits}(R',v)\,u^{-1}$ for a unit $u$. Then there exist maps $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ with each $e(\gamma)$ over $A_0.f$, and $\deg, K : \Gamma_t \to \mathbb{N}$, $x : \Gamma_t \to R$, such that $x(\gamma) = r^{K(\gamma)}\,(u^{-1}\gamma u)$, $e(\gamma) = E(\tau(x(\gamma)))$, $r^{K(\gamma)} \equiv 1 \pmod n$; each pair $(e(\gamma), e'(\gamma))$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg(\gamma)}$ from $A_0$ to itself (both morphisms are group-law homomorphisms commuting with the $\Lambda$-action and composing in either order to the action of $r^{\deg(\gamma)}$) and $e(\gamma)$ preserves the level structure; for all $\gamma, \gamma'$ there are $i, j$ with $e(\gamma\gamma')$ followed by the action of $r^i$ equal to $e(\gamma')$ followed by $e(\gamma)$ followed by the action of $r^j$; if $\gamma$ is the integer scalar $c$ then $e(\gamma)$ followed by the action of $r^i$ is the action of $c\,r^i$ for some $i$; conversely, if $e(\gamma)$ followed by the action of some $r^i$ equals the action of some positive integer, then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar; and finally every $y \in M_2(O)$ which commutes with $j(\Lambda)$, admits $y' \in M_2(O)$ with $yy' = y'y = r^{dd}$, and for which $E(y)$ preserves the level, satisfies $E(y)$ followed by the action of $r^i$ equals $e(\gamma)$ followed by the action of $r^j$, for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ and some $i, j$.
--
--   This is the construction, at a fixed base point $A_0$, of the dictionary between the quaternionic unit group $\Gamma_t$ and level-preserving self-isogenies of the fake elliptic curve: the group law on $\Gamma_t$ is matched with composition up to multiplication by powers of $r$, scalars are matched with multiplication endomorphisms, and all level-preserving endomorphisms of $r$-power degree commuting with the $\Lambda$-action are accounted for. It feeds the construction of the fake elliptic curve carrying a formal module of height four with a full endomorphism dictionary on the Čerednik–Drinfeld side.
